      "Shireen laughed and cried at the same time. Then she read the note again. You always look in boxes for things that are not in boxes. It sounded like a riddle, and her grandmother had loved riddles more than anything. She thought about the games they played when she was small — riddles at breakfast, riddles on the balcony, riddles instead of goodnight stories.",
